# onnxruntime-node's linux-x64 postinstall downloads a CUDA package from
# nuget.org. It is not optional-and-quiet: when the fetch fails it ROLLS BACK
# node_modules, which has destroyed this repo's install before. The CPU
# execution provider — the only one this app uses — ships in the base package,
# so skipping the download costs nothing and is also required by the offline
# rule, which forbids fetching anything at build or run time.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
